l\\r\\n\\r\\n* add rsync for build\\r\\n\\r\\n* add all-in-one docker\\r\\n\\r\\n* update prepare scripts\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update swe_env_box.py\\r\\n\\r\\n* Add swe_entry.sh \\\\(buggy now\\\\)\\r\\n\\r\\n* Parse the test command in swe_entry.sh\\r\\n\\r\\n* Update README for instance eval in sandbox\\r\\n\\r\\n* revert specialized config\\r\\n\\r\\n* replace run_as_devin as an init arg\\r\\n\\r\\n* set container & run_as_root via args\\r\\n\\r\\n* update swe entry script\\r\\n\\r\\n* update env\\r\\n\\r\\n* remove mounting\\r\\n\\r\\n* allow error after swe_entry\\r\\n\\r\\n* update swe_env_box\\r\\n\\r\\n* move file\\r\\n\\r\\n* update gitignore\\r\\n\\r\\n* get swe_env_box a working demo\\r\\n\\r\\n* support faking user response & provide sandox ahead of time;\\r\\nalso return state for controller\\r\\n\\r\\n* tweak main to support adding controller kwargs\\r\\n\\r\\n* add module\\r\\n\\r\\n* initialize plugin for provided sandbox\\r\\n\\r\\n* add pip cache to plugin & fix jupyter kernel waiting\\r\\n\\r\\n* better print Observation output\\r\\n\\r\\n* add run infer scripts\\r\\n\\r\\n* update readme\\r\\n\\r\\n* add utility for ge...\") |   \\n  \\n[ **README.md** ](/root/openhands/-/blob/main/evaluation/README.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n#  <::after> Evaluation \\n\\nThis folder contains code and resources to run experiments and evaluations. \\n\\n##  <::after> Logistics \\n\\nTo better organize the evaluation folder, we should follow the rules below: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Each subfolder contains a specific benchmark or experiment. For example, ` evaluation/swe_bench ` should contain all the preprocessing/evaluation/analysis scripts. \\n  * <::marker>Raw data and experimental records should not be stored within this repo. \\n  * <::marker>For model outputs, they should be stored at [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization. \\n  * <::marker>Important data files of manageable size and analysis scripts (e.g., jupyter notebooks) can be directly uploaded to this repo. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Supported Benchmarks \\n\\nTo learn more about how to integrate your benchmark into OpenHands, check out [ tutorial here ](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/evaluation-harness) . \\n\\n###  <::after> Software Engineering \\n\\n  * <::marker>SWE-Bench: [ ` evaluation/swe_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/swe_bench)\\n  * <::marker>HumanEvalFix: [ ` evaluation/humanevalfix ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/humanevalfix)\\n  * <::marker>BIRD: [ ` evaluation/bird ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/bird)\\n  * <::marker>BioCoder: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>ML-Bench: [ ` evaluation/ml_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/ml_bench)\\n  * <::marker>APIBench: [ ` evaluation/gorilla ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gorilla)\\n  * <::marker>ToolQA: [ ` evaluation/toolqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/toolqa)\\n  * <::marker>AiderBench: [ ` evaluation/aider_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/aider_bench)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Web Browsing \\n\\n  * <::marker>WebArena: [ ` evaluation/webarena ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/webarena)\\n  * <::marker>MiniWob++: [ ` evaluation/miniwob ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/miniwob)\\n\\n\\n\\n###  <::after> Misc. Assistance \\n\\n  * <::marker>GAIA: [ ` evaluation/gaia ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gaia)\\n  * <::marker>GPQA: [ ` evaluation/gpqa ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/gpqa)\\n  * <::marker>AgentBench: [ ` evaluation/agent_bench ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/agent_bench)\\n  * <::marker>MINT: [ ` evaluation/mint ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/mint)\\n  * <::marker>Entity deduction Arena (EDA): [ ` evaluation/EDA ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/EDA)\\n  * <::marker>ProofWriter: [ ` evaluation/logic_reasoning ` ](/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation/logic_reasoning)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Before everything begins: Setup Environment and LLM Configuration \\n\\nPlease follow instruction [ here ](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md) to setup your local development environment and LLM. \\n\\nOpenHands in development mode uses ` config.toml ` to keep track of most configurations. \\n\\nHere\\'s an example configuration file you can use to define and use multiple LLMs: \\n    \\n    \\n    [llm]\\n    # IMPORTANT: add your API key here, and set the model to the one you want to evaluate\\n    model = \"gpt-4o-2024-05-13\"\\n    api_key = \"sk-XXX\"\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_gpt4_1106_preview_llm]\\n    model = \"gpt-4-1106-preview\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n    \\n    [llm.eval_some_openai_compatible_model_llm]\\n    model = \"openai/MODEL_NAME\"\\n    base_url = \"https://OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_URL/v1\"\\n    api_key = \"XXX\"\\n    temperature = 0.0\\n\\n###  <::after> Result Visualization \\n\\nCheck [ this huggingface space ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) for visualization of existing experimental results. \\n\\n###  <::after> Upload your results \\n\\nYou can start your own fork of [ our huggingface evaluation outputs ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation) and submit a PR of your evaluation results to our hosted huggingface repo via PR following the guide [ here ](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/en/repositories-pull-requests-discussions#pull-requests-and-discussions) . \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\ngorilla \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation?ref_type=heads', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251103_024556_779724.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/tree/main/evaluation?re